<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hyderabad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hyderabad is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musi-river">Musi River</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>, now the capital of the Indian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a>. It was founded around 1591 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-quli-qutb-shah">Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golconda-fort">Golconda</a>, who built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charminar">Charminar</a>, and from 1763 it was the capital of the Nizams of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad-sindh">Hyderabad</a>. It is now one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s largest cities and a centre of information technology.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hyderabad.jpg" alt="Hyderabad" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: iMahesh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Durgam_cheruvu_and_Hitech_CIty.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
